design:
One pkg/sandbox type consulted by every tool, with a per-profile config block:
  sandbox: {mode: off|policy|bwrap, allow_write: [...], allow_net: [...], require_confirm: [shell, write_file, hashline_patch], env_allow: [...]}
Decision is Allow/Deny/Confirm, so the same layer serves both A (deny dangerous shapes) and B (escalate to OS isolation). Confirmation rides ADK tool/toolconfirmation (adk_request_confirmation round-trips through FunctionResponse) and gets one rendering per transport: TUI modal, web prompt, (later) chat inline keyboard. Deny returns a tool error the model can route around, it does not kill the turn.
